cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: arithmetica
abstract: >-
  Exact geometric predicates for f64 input in Rust. The crate implements
  Shewchuk's adaptive-precision orientation, in-circle and in-sphere tests,
  and adds exact comparisons of distances and angles: which of two points is
  nearer to a third, whether an angle is acute, right or obtuse, and whether
  a point lies within a given distance of another point or of a segment.
  Each returns the exact sign for every finite f64 input, across the whole
  binary64 range. Exact line-intersection points, their exact comparison and
  the expansion arithmetic underneath complete the crate, which is no_std
  and has no dependencies.
